  {
    "objectID": "examples/svgs-js.html#not-yet-supported",
    "href": "examples/svgs-js.html#not-yet-supported",
    "title": "OJS SVG Magic Move Demo",
    "section": "Not Yet Supported",
    "text": "Not Yet Supported\nNone of the sequences on this page currently animate — every transition below hard-cuts instead of morphing. D3, Observable Plot, and Vega-Lite (via {ojs}) all produce fully compatible SVG shapes (&lt;circle&gt;, &lt;rect&gt;, &lt;path&gt;, &lt;line&gt;, &lt;text&gt;), but Quarto’s Observable JS cells render after Reveal’s ready event, while this extension only scans for SVG content once, synchronously, at ready. So the SVG magic-move feature never activates for {ojs}-rendered charts, regardless of shape compatibility. Kept here as a reference for what real {ojs}-rendered SVG looks like, pending a fix upstream."
  },
